[page mode=document title="WASM effects"]

  [heading level=1 fg=bright-cyan]WASM effects[/heading]
  [link href="/"][text dim]< back to index[/text][/link]
  [spacer lines=1 /]

  [text]An effect is a WebAssembly module the site serves alongside its pages.
  The client runs it in a sandbox with a fuel budget and a memory cap, and with
  no imports beyond drawing: it cannot read files, open sockets, or reach the
  page it is drawing on.[/text]
  [spacer lines=1 /]

  [box border=rounded fg=yellow title="Build the modules first"]
    [text]This page references [text bold]/effects/*.wasm[/text]. Run
    [text bold]make effects[/text] in the dustnet repository and copy the
    modules you want beside this page. A missing module degrades to a static
    page rather than failing the load.[/text]
  [/box]
  [spacer lines=1 /]

  [heading level=2 fg=yellow]Full-region background[/heading]
  [animate background=true id="backdrop" src="/effects/starfield.wasm" fps=20 loop=true /]
  [spacer lines=1 /]

  [heading level=2 fg=yellow]Bounded region[/heading]
  [box w=48 h=8 border=single fg=white title="static_noise"]
    [animate id="noise" src="/effects/static_noise.wasm" fps=12 loop=true /]
  [/box]
[/page]
